WEBVTT

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:11.820
Since we got here it's just been
"basics, basics, basics"!

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:15.740
That's all we've done, every single class
since we started here!

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.290
And the Phantom's class is the worst!

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:20.790
We could ask for something different.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.460
Let's ask Andou-<i>sensei</i>!

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:57.510
A Glimpse of Stardom

00:01:54.430 --> 00:02:01.060
Today, we'll be talking about the
Stanislavski technique and how to--

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:05.940
Why do you all look dead?

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:09.150
Andou-<i>sensei</i>! Can I make a suggestion?

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.070
She's doing it.

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:12.240
She's actually asking.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:15.200
What are you girls plotting?

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.870
Shoot, Watanabe.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:17.910
Thanks!

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:23.910
So, there's one crucial skill that
every other teacher has mentioned to us.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.500
Expression!

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:28.040
Expression.

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:30.750
<i>Expression!</i>

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:35.180
I knew who every teacher was
without her even saying their names.

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:36.010
And?

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:39.390
<i>And </i>I believe the one class
where we'll learn

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:42.520
<i>how </i>to express ourselves is this one.

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.680
We've been Kouka students for four months,

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:48.480
so we think it might be nice if we, well,

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:52.150
had a little opportunity to actually <i>act</i>.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:58.870
Is that your suggestion?

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:05.370
Well, I've been here eight years, and the
first-year's curriculum has never changed.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:09.830
First-year students are expected to sit
politely and learn the basics of acting.

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:13.420
That's how it's been done at
the Kouka School for a century now.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:17.550
But here's an idea, Watanabe!
Do that again.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:18.510
Huh?

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:21.890
Show me what I sound like
when I say "expression."

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:24.890
If I think it's good,
I'll consider your suggestion.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.600
Those are high stakes!

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:32.230
Got a lot of pressure on me,
but here goes...

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:37.740
Expression? What's that,
some hot new band?

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:43.290
Okay, open your textbooks.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:44.580
That's it.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:46.790
So much for that.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:49.500
Sorry I couldn't help.

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:50.790
Actually, Sara--

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:55.340
Watanabe-<i>san</i>, that was a good
impression of Andou-<i>sensei</i>.

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:56.550
It so was!

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:59.470
Maybe it was <i>too </i>good.

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:03.600
Oh, Watanabe-<i>san</i>!

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.470
There's a package here for you.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:12.730
13, 14, 15, 16 roses.

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:15.480
Sara-- Watanabe-<i>san</i>, is today...

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:19.030
Yep! I turn 16 years old today!

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:20.280
Huh?!

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:21.990
Today's your birthday?!

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:24.030
Why didn't you tell us?!

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.660
Happy birthday!

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:28.540
Aww, thanks!

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:32.130
My first friend's birthday is today...

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:35.670
So who gave you this bouquet of roses?

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:37.380
Is it a guy?!

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.050
Ohmigosh, your boyfriend?!

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:42.930
Maybe! He lives in Tokyo,
so we're long-distance right now,

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:44.970
but it could be him!

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:49.270
A-And he's a real, live person?

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:50.770
Not some anime guy?

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:55.480
Is that the person
you're always messaging?

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:02.150
Happy Birthday

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:02.150
from your fan
 of the red rose

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:02.280
What the hell? That's kind of creepy.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:07.080
Sara-- Watanabe-<i>san</i>, does your boyfriend
like these sorts of gestures?

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:09.580
That's hard to say.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:12.160
Kouzaburou

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:14.750
You sure are in a good mood.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:20.590
Why wouldn't I be?
It's my darling Sarasa's 16th birthday.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:23.010
You knew that, right, Akiya?

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.340
Of course I did!

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:30.020
So, did you send her a present?
You <i>are </i>her boyfriend, right?

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:34.600
I'm gonna give it to her
when she comes home this summer.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:40.940
C'mon, where's your passion?
I sent her a bouquet of 16 roses.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:44.240
She's so incredibly special to me.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.950
And this is her special day.

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:48.620
Wait... hold on.

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:53.080
Don't worry, I didn't say it was from me.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:56.840
I said it was from
her "fan of the red rose."

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:59.000
Happy Birthday

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:59.000
from your fan of the red rose

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:59.210
Her fan of the red rose?

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:04.380
Forget summer vacation. Why not just
send her something now?

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:08.220
I'll send her a text message tonight.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:11.470
You gonna stop by her grandpa's
place tonight again?

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:13.560
Yeah, that's the plan.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.520
Happy Birthday, Sarasa-<i>chan</i>! I'll give you
your present over summer break!

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:24.030
Her boyfriend's a frog? And a bot at that.

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:26.320
But why does a bot have a private account?

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:31.490
I won't let that frog outdo me.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:35.670
I wanna give Watanabe-<i>san </i>something
she'll love even more than those roses.

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:39.210
After all, she's the first
friend I ever made.

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:44.090
And now's the perfect chance
to call her by her first name.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:46.550
Should I add -<i>chan </i>because
she's younger than me?

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:49.550
Sarasa-<i>tan</i>? Saracchi?

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:52.350
Or do I keep it simple with Sarasa?

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:54.350
Oh, geez!

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:58.150
Oh my God!

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:04.610
The hardest-to-get lottery prize figurine
of Tsukahara Vault Taku!

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:07.660
Oh, Taku-<i>sama</i>!

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:13.040
Ai-<i>chan</i>, you got this for me,
didn't you?! I could cry!

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:16.710
I tried four times to win it
and only won hand towels!

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:17.960
Well, Sara--

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:21.420
Watanabe-<i>san</i>, you're always
going on and on about <i>Floor Kings</i>,

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:24.380
so I gave it a go and won the top prize.

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:26.090
In one try?!

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:28.390
No, after a half-dozen tries.

00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:29.300
You like it?

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:31.430
I love it!

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:32.970
Especially this part!

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:35.980
"To Sarasa. Sorry it's late.
Happy birthday."

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:37.390
Don't read it out loud!

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:39.690
But look!

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:41.230
"To Sarasa"!

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:44.730
Look, Sa... Watanabe-<i>san</i>.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:50.070
Just call me Sarasa!
We're friends, aren't we, Ai-<i>chan</i>?

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:54.700
Sarasa.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:08:00.960
Oh, Taku-<i>sama</i>! Ai-<i>chan </i>called me "Sarasa"!

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:02.920
I can die happy now!

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:05.460
Oh, right.

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:08.220
I had a meeting with
the other teachers yesterday,

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:11.720
and they said we could
change up the curriculum.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:13.220
Quiet down.

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:16.560
We're going to perform a scene from
Shakespeare's <i>Romeo and Juliet</i>.

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:19.390
The roles are Romeo, Juliet,

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:24.360
Tybalt, and Juliet's Nurse.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:28.240
Each group of four will have two weeks
to prepare their scene on their own.

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:29.070
There you go.

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:30.200
On our own?

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:33.490
Andou-<i>sensei</i>, what do you mean
by "on our own"?

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:34.870
Is this not a class activity?

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:36.410
We got duped.

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:37.910
Some teacher he is.

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:43.250
Now, now, I <i>did </i>have to fight a bit
in that faculty meeting.

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:47.630
They let us do this under the assumption
that this would be an experiment.

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:52.340
So I haven't prepared any materials
or plans for guiding you to perform.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:55.640
You'll rehearse on your own,
then in two weeks,

00:08:55.640 --> 00:09:00.270
we'll spend one class period
presenting our scenes,

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:03.860
and I'll give you <i>thorough</i>
feedback on your performances.

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:08.110
Also, since this was your idea,

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:11.950
you won't complain if we end up
using it for next year's class, right?

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:13.450
Crafty bastard.

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:15.580
Of course, we don't have to do it.

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:17.160
We'll do it!

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:22.920
We drew lots to determine
who'd be in each of the five groups.

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:23.960
Group E.

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:26.870
Group E

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:26.870
Sarasa Watanabe

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:26.870
Hoshino Kaoru

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:26.870
Chika Sawada

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:28.420
Guess we're with you, Sarasa.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:31.720
Yep! Let's break a leg, Group E!

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:33.680
How do we wanna pick roles?

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:38.430
Sarasa and I both want to be <i>otoko-yaku</i>,
so we'll pick between Romeo and Tybalt.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:39.720
Rock-paper-scissors?

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:40.600
Sure!

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:44.020
Then Naracchi and I will play
the <i>musume-yaku </i>parts!

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:45.690
Want to do rock-paper-scissors, too?

00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:46.520
Sure.

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:48.020
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:50.740
Sweet! I'll take Romeo!

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:53.320
That means I'm Tybalt!

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:54.240
What about you two?

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:57.240
Rock, paper, scissors!
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:05.580
Um, I'll play, uh, Ju...

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:06.460
Juliet's Nurse!

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:07.290
Huh?

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:12.720
I mean, I wanted to play that! A comic
role will be the perfect challenge!

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:14.840
You'll make a better Juliet
than me, anyway, Naracchi.

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:18.390
Really? I can play Juliet?!

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:20.060
Of course!

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:24.020
I've always <i>loved </i>the Kouka version
of Juliet! I'm so happy right now!

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:24.020
Oh, it's fine.

00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:26.440
I wanted to play the Nurse, anyway!

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:29.190
Okay. Then Naracchi's our Juliet.

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:30.230
Yep.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:35.360
Tatami Room

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:37.700
Let's start with a quick readthrough.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:41.450
To be honest, I think Sarasa
would be better off as Romeo

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:43.540
instead of the darker Tybalt.

00:10:44.710 --> 00:10:48.340
Especially after that evening when
we were walking back from the theater,

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:53.470
and she recited those few
perfect lines as Romeo...

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:55.130
Okay, you start, Chika.

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:56.760
Got it!

00:10:56.760 --> 00:11:03.390
Madam, your mother craves a word with you.

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:06.230
Good woman! Who is her mother?

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:11.520
Why sir, her mother is the lady
of the house, Lady Capulet.

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:15.030
A Capulet?! O dear account!

00:11:15.030 --> 00:11:15.950
She's up next.

00:11:15.950 --> 00:11:19.660
Show me the passion that's
driving you to become a top star.

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:21.620
Show us all you've got!

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:27.170
That voice, is that Romeo?
Romeo, of house Montague?

00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:34.880
How dare the man come hither,
to the Cap... Capulet? Mansion itself...

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:36.170
How are you this bad?!

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:37.720
S-Sorry!

00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:40.180
Stop messing around and get serious!

00:11:40.180 --> 00:11:43.060
I-I wasn't messing around.

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:45.270
Whatever! We don't have time for this.

00:11:45.270 --> 00:11:47.140
Juliet, your lines are next!

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:57.950
See?! Your crappy reading
threw Naracchi off!

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:01.950
My, what are you all doing here?

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:03.490
Good morning, Senpai!

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:06.080
What's this about? Some secret meeting?

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:10.920
Just kidding! Andou-<i>sensei </i>filled us
all in on your little scene exercise.

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:16.510
You first-years are already getting
to act? Boy, you girls are lucky!

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:20.470
And you're doing <i>Romeo and Juliet</i>?
I love that show!

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:25.060
One thing, though: you really can't
use this room to practice, mmkay?

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:27.760
First-Year Lockers

00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:29.350
Hijiri-<i>senpai </i>was really mad at us.

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:31.690
She was? But she was all smiles.

00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:35.320
That's how you can tell when
she's angry--she's <i>smiling</i>!

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:37.690
Ugh, we can't use the tatami room anymore.

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:40.410
Where should we practice
from now on, then, Kaoru?

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:45.830
Group A's using the lecture hall,
but they might let us share it.

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:49.290
Hey, can we use half
the lecture hall with you?

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:50.250
I don't see why not.

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:51.000
Sure.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:51.790
Yeah.

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:53.130
W-We can't!

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:54.290
Why not?

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:58.670
W-We're doing the same scene,
so we'll throw each other off!

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:02.220
I don't wanna share a place
to practice with another group!

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:07.270
Then where do we practice?
All the other rooms are already taken.

00:13:07.270 --> 00:13:10.020
Why don't we just do it
out on the sidewalk?

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:10.980
What?

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:13.730
The sidewalk?! Are you insane?!

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:18.440
We are students of the 100th class
of the <i>esteemed </i>Kouka School!

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:23.570
We can't perform on the sidewalk!
What a way to ruin Kouka for everyone!

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:27.870
We might be students now, but we are
destined to be professionals!

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:30.160
You'd better drill that
into your skull, got it?!

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:35.960
I have to use the bathroom.

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:39.710
That scared me.

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:43.340
Who pissed her off? You <i>know</i>
she's got a really short fuse.

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:45.050
I wouldn't say that.

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:50.430
Her mom was a Kouka actress,
and her grandma was a top <i>musume-yaku</i>.

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:53.020
I can't imagine the kind of pressure
that puts on her.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:56.020
Hoshino-<i>san</i>.

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:03.450
Yeah, I know. I'm a loudmouth
with a short fuse, sorry.

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:07.280
There was a girl like you in JPX.

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:09.790
She was our group leader
and was always angry.

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:13.960
What, you come to rub it in?

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:18.670
I never went to high school, and barely
went to elementary and middle school.

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:24.680
So Sarasa wasn't the reason I couldn't
read Juliet's lines this morning.

00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:26.050
I...

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:28.680
...can't read kanji.

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:35.930
"Favorite Place: beech"
"Why: Its suthing"

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:36.190
Back in JPX, I was used to my manager
writing the readings down for me.

00:14:36.190 --> 00:14:40.780
This morning was the first time
I realized how screwed I am.

00:14:40.780 --> 00:14:43.280
None of us have any experience,

00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:47.620
so unless you get mad at us,
we'll just end up holding you back.

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:50.410
What the hell? That's so not fair.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:53.620
What if I don't want to be
the bad guy, huh?

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:57.460
Then Group E fails together.

00:14:57.460 --> 00:14:59.130
Is that a threat?!

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:01.960
{=0}Nono Park

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:04.340
Ta-dah! Well? Isn't it perfect?

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:06.380
It's not the sidewalk, that's for sure!

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:09.930
Chika-<i>chan </i>and I looked all over
for a good spot to practice!

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:12.020
Will this work, Kaoru?

00:15:12.020 --> 00:15:14.100
Not like we can go anywhere else.

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:19.900
Okay, we've got two weeks to prep this
scene that's not gonna teach us anything.

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:21.190
C'mon, Group E!

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:22.900
Let's do this!

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:25.240
Really, Sugimoto-<i>san</i>?

00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:28.620
You're gonna lend me your Blu-ray of
Winter Troupe <i>Romeo and Juliet</i>?

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:30.530
Kaoru asked me to.

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:33.580
She said if you don't level up, and fast,

00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:37.250
then "Group E's gonna drag
the rest of our class down with them."

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:41.210
That Hoshino-<i>san </i>doesn't mince words, huh!

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:42.880
Ai-<i>chan</i>!

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:47.340
Sugimoto-<i>san </i>lent me her copy
of <i>Romeo and Juliet</i>! Wanna watch?

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:51.180
I'm good. I gotta spend all night
writing kanji readings onto our script.

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:51.130
Kanji Dictionary

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:55.680
Okay! Could I borrow your
Blu-ray player and headphones?

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:57.390
Sure.

00:15:57.390 --> 00:16:01.730
I'm gonna study so hard, I'm gonna
knock the socks off Hoshino-<i>san</i>!

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:02.730
Mmkay.

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:05.190
Let's do an awesome job tomorrow morning!

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:06.240
Yep.

00:16:07.450 --> 00:16:12.330
I wonder where the Sarasa
I saw that day disappeared to.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:15.450
That voice, is that Romeo?

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:18.370
Romeo, of house Montague?

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:23.590
How dare the man come hither,
to the Capulet mansion itself!

00:16:23.590 --> 00:16:26.050
Such sins shall not be endured!

00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:28.840
Such sins shall not be endured.

00:16:30.970 --> 00:16:34.430
So, how's your Group E looking, Kaoru?

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:35.970
And by that, I mean, how's Sarasa?

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:38.520
I kinda don't know.

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:40.230
Like, it's kind of creepy.

00:16:40.230 --> 00:16:41.730
Creepy how?

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:45.400
You know how you're supposed to
improve little by little?

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:47.820
Sarasa just...

00:16:53.910 --> 00:16:55.580
I'm so nervous.

00:16:55.580 --> 00:17:00.370
It's okay. Andou-<i>sensei </i>doesn't
expect us to be good.

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:04.540
Then why did the Phantom
even want us to do this?

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:07.300
Probably because he wanted
to see how much fun we'd have,

00:17:07.300 --> 00:17:10.590
or how much effort we'd put into it?

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:11.840
Seriously?

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:15.970
I mean, isn't playing pretend
way more fun when you've got friends?

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:18.730
We only had two weeks
to put this together,

00:17:18.730 --> 00:17:21.060
but I'm sure that even when I
finally get to play Lady Oscar,

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:25.570
I'll remember these last two weeks.

00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:28.820
Enough about Oscar. That <i>was </i>fun, though.

00:17:28.820 --> 00:17:30.360
It doesn't matter if we mess up.

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:33.620
Just keep going until the end.

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:36.280
But give it your all, okay?!

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:39.500
Yeah! We'll give it 100% to the very end!

00:17:39.500 --> 00:17:41.870
Okay, each group gets
15 minutes to perform.

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:45.960
I've marked out the 'stage' with tape,
so use that as a guide.

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:47.420
Group A is first...

00:17:47.420 --> 00:17:51.380
...most of the time,
so let's go with Group E.

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:53.640
We have to go <i>first</i>?!

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:56.850
We didn't even think about
the size of the actual stage.

00:17:56.850 --> 00:17:59.980
Okay, let's imagine it now!

00:17:59.980 --> 00:18:02.600
There's a balcony up above,

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:04.850
and a big ballroom in the center.

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:06.940
The lights are tinged with blue,

00:18:06.940 --> 00:18:10.240
and there's a crescent moon
through the window.

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:12.320
What beauty!

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:17.740
She shines like
a rich jewel amidst the crowd!

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:20.870
Love! This, truly, is love!

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:24.790
My life's road has led me
to her beautiful flame!

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:24.790
C'mon, now.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:27.340
Stop trying to gauge my reaction.

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:30.260
Keep looking at me,
and you'll flub your lines.

00:18:30.260 --> 00:18:33.050
Good woman! Who is her mother?

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:39.060
Why sir, her mother is the
lady of the house, Lady Capulet.

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:39.060
She sure is spry for an old lady.

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:42.980
Her daughter is a visage of beauty,
and intelligent, too!

00:18:42.980 --> 00:18:46.100
How fortunate I am to have nursed her!

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:49.900
She is a visage of beauty, and...

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:51.360
I messed up!

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:56.950
Oh, no, I'm gonna cry!

00:18:56.950 --> 00:18:58.490
It doesn't matter if we mess up.

00:18:58.490 --> 00:19:02.540
Just keep going until the end.

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:03.750
Oh, my goodness!

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:07.210
I felt those qualities of such importance,
I said them twice!

00:19:08.670 --> 00:19:10.130
Nice save.

00:19:10.130 --> 00:19:13.840
My! Come hither, nurse!
Where goeth yonder gentleman?

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:16.510
The man with visage radiant as the sun!

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:21.010
I can tell she's had experience
being on a big stage before.

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:23.680
There, him now who is going out of door!

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:23.680
But boy, this Juliet...

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:26.270
...is <i>so </i>not in love.

00:19:26.270 --> 00:19:30.650
Go ask his name, if he be married...

00:19:26.270 --> 00:19:30.650
Still, she keeps looking at me.

00:19:30.650 --> 00:19:33.400
And not how Hoshino was.

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:37.490
My only love, sprung from my only hate.

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:37.490
Hold on, Narata...

00:19:37.490 --> 00:19:40.660
Are you performing for
an audience of <i>one</i>?

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:44.700
Okay, next up, our Kouka misfit,
Sarasa Watanabe.

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:44.530
Group E Roles

00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:49.080
That voice, is that Romeo?

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:51.460
Romeo, of house Montague?!

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:56.880
How dare the man come hither,
to the Capulet mansion itself!

00:19:56.880 --> 00:19:59.010
She's directing her gaze
at the balcony seats.

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:02.140
And she's keeping her eyes at a 45-degree
angle so the lights will catch them.

00:20:02.140 --> 00:20:03.270
Impressive.

00:20:03.270 --> 00:20:06.850
Fetch me my rapier, boy!

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:09.770
That Romeo...

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:12.480
...is naught but a villain.

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:18.700
Sarasa Watanabe was reborn overnight.

00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:22.530
And because today, she has an audience,

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:23.950
it's even more--

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:27.580
Okay! Good job, Group E.

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:31.920
Here's a question for you.
Who did you imagine as your audience?

00:20:31.920 --> 00:20:33.550
The people in this room right now.

00:20:33.550 --> 00:20:36.260
I-I didn't think about it.

00:20:36.260 --> 00:20:38.510
A full house with balcony seats!

00:20:38.510 --> 00:20:39.800
One person.

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:42.680
So that's why you were
staring at me that whole time?

00:20:42.680 --> 00:20:43.560
Yes.

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:47.430
In JPX, they told us that even if
we only had an audience of one,

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:52.150
we should direct our performance
towards them and give it our all.

00:20:52.150 --> 00:20:54.270
That's a good thought,

00:20:54.270 --> 00:21:00.700
but the Kouka theater holds 2,500 people,
and every performance is a full house.

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:05.450
When you're acting, you should act
for every one of those 2,500 people!

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:06.540
Got it!

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:10.420
Also, Narata, if you're going to play
a <i>musume-yaku</i>, try to be a little sweeter.

00:21:10.420 --> 00:21:13.790
This is the first time I've seen
a Juliet who didn't smile.

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:15.210
Next, Chika Sawada!

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:16.460
Yes, sir!

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:20.510
Great recovery after
you flubbed your line there.

00:21:20.510 --> 00:21:24.390
But hunching over doesn't
make you an old woman.

00:21:24.390 --> 00:21:26.350
Use that imagination.

00:21:26.350 --> 00:21:27.810
Yes, sir.

00:21:27.810 --> 00:21:28.850
Next up, Hoshino.

00:21:28.850 --> 00:21:29.680
Sir!

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:32.560
Don't let your mind stray
when you're performing.

00:21:32.560 --> 00:21:34.520
Leave yourself behind
when you step on stage.

00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:35.440
Okay, next!

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:37.610
Wait, is that it?

00:21:37.610 --> 00:21:39.690
For now, yeah.

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:42.280
You haven't learned any skills yet,

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:46.120
so I want you to act
however you want for now.

00:21:46.120 --> 00:21:50.120
Don't get too hung up on my critique.

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:51.670
Right, last up, Watanabe.

00:21:51.670 --> 00:21:53.170
Yes, sir!

00:21:53.170 --> 00:21:55.840
Your impression was uncanny.

00:21:55.840 --> 00:21:58.630
I'll admit, I was shocked.

00:21:58.630 --> 00:22:01.050
But I'm sorry, Watanabe,

00:22:01.050 --> 00:22:04.050
you'll never be a top star.

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:11.520
If you don't change, you'll never be
a top star of the Kouka Revue.

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:46.980
Act 7: 
